# Pearl UI

Source of truth: `DESIGN.md`. Identity comes from account manager's Pearl system, adapted to this Next.js app. Do not invent a second look.

- Colours are `--rd-*` tokens in `apps/web/app/globals.css`, both light and dark. No raw hex in components or new CSS. A new colour is a new token in both themes.
- Primary action is ink (`--rd-primary-bg`). Logo red (`--rd-accent`) is one accent per screen, never an error. Errors use `--rd-danger`.
- Status is a badge with a label: paid / pending / danger / neutral. Do not signal status by colour alone.
- Type: IBM Plex Sans Arabic for body, Noto Kufi Arabic for headings, Inter Tight tabular figures for numbers and money. No new Google Font link.
- Reuse the shell, page header, card, table, and button classes in `DESIGN.md`. Do not add a new card, button, or table style for one page.
- RTL first: logical properties (`margin-inline`, `text-align: start`). Touch targets at least 44px. Motion 150–450ms, transform and opacity only.
- The existing `--bg` / `--accent` blue tokens are legacy. New and touched UI uses `--rd-*` only. Do not extend the blue set.
